Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: PPE diagnostics for the PON uplink (debugfs)

NOT FOR UPSTREAM - diagnostic build for XG-040G-MF.

Adds debugfs below /sys/kernel/debug/ppe/:
- diag:    per-ingress histogram of RX PPE cpu reasons and of the FOE
           entry state at the reported hash (hardware readback for SRAM,
           sampled 1/4); write 0/1 to disable/enable, reset to clear
- trace:   capture up to N packets matching a src/dst/proto filter with
           FOE words, descriptor msg0/msg1 and the frame head. The IPv4
           header is located by ethertype so 802.1Q-tagged and PPPoE
           frames coming from the PON are matched as well
- reg:     single FE register read ("<off>") / modify ("<off> <mask> <val>")
- regdump: PPE/GDM/CDM configuration registers and GDM hardware MIB counters
- foe:     read ("<hash>") or patch ("<hash> <word> <mask> <val>") a FOE
- npu_init: re-run the NPU HWNAT init with explicit init_info
           ("<wan_mode> <ppe_type> <wan_sel> <max_packet> <cds>
             <xpon_hal_api> <wan_xsi> <ct_joyme4>") or "deinit"
- npu_fw:  load another NPU firmware pair from /lib/firmware/ and reboot
           the NPU cores

airoha_npu_ppe_init() now shares its mailbox code with the npu_init knob
so wan_mode (hardwired to QDMA_WAN_ETHER) can be varied at runtime.

Signed-off-by: zhoufla <zhoufla@users.noreply.github.com>
---
